.06379215390721615, "r7": -2.6148530125894798}, "sol": {"r0": 0.20273694880892368, "r1": 1.0221321169116449, "r7": -7.889846257813815}}], "n_events": 218, "method": "Move = prior UTC daily close -> close on event day (r0), next day (r1), +7 days (r7). FOMC hikes/cuts dated from changes in the FRED target-range upper bound (DFEDTARU, effective the day after the announcement), holds from the Fed meeting calendar (covers recent years only). NFP/CPI \"hot\" or \"cold\" = the released m/m change vs the median of the prior 12 months, a crude proxy because free consensus forecasts do not exist. Uses today's revised data, not the first print.", "caveats": ["Release dates: FRED's calendar only covers 2025 onward. Earlier jobs-report dates are computed from the BLS scheduling rule (it matched every official 2025-26 date except shutdown delays). CPI events are 2025+ only.", "Small samples: e.g. only a handful of hikes/cuts since 2015, and SOL history starts mid-2021.", "Regimes overlap: crypto-specific news (ETFs, halvings, hacks) dominates many of these days.", "Daily closes in UTC: a 2pm ET FOMC decision and an 8:30am ET jobs report land inside one candle with everything else that day.", "\"Hot/cold\" is vs trailing trend, not vs Wall Street consensus (consensus data needs a paid feed, e.g. Trading Economics or Bloomberg).", "FRED data are revised: payroll changes here are the latest vintage, not what markets saw at release (ALFRED first-release data needs a free FRED API key).", "Descriptive statistics only. Not a trading signal or financial advice."]}